t remains the prerequisite graph. Validate referenced courses separately."}] [#edb/ref 1001 :course-group/title {:db/doc "Catalog group title, for example High School - Traditional or Mathematical Foundations."}] [#edb/ref 1002 :course-group/id {:db/doc "Stable identity of this course group."}] [#edb/ref 1003 :course/next {:db/doc "Optional direct downstream courses for curriculum navigation. Ordinary refs preserve shared courses; reverse lookup supplies preceding courses. These links present progression between topic collections. Topic/next remains the authoritative prerequisite graph; course links do not impose additional whole-course completion requirements."}] [#edb/ref 1004 :course/outcomes {:db/doc "Optional owned course outcomes, defined in 2-2-course-outcome.edn. Sort by course-outcome/index for display order; each outcome may have a category heading. Writers must separately ensure course-outcome/validate on each outcome."}] [#edb/ref 1005 :course/units {:db/doc "Units belonging to this course. At least one is required when course/validate is explicitly ensured. These ordinary refs define unordered membership; unit/next supplies navigation between units. Topic/next supplies the underlying knowledge dependencies. Referenced units must be validated separately."}] [#edb/ref 1006 :course-outcome/index {:db/doc "1-based display order across all outcomes in the course, continuing across category headings. Must be positive and unique within that course, not globally unique."}] [#edb/ref 1007 :course/title {:db/doc "Course title without its code, for example Algebra I or Vector Calculus II."}] [#edb/ref 1008 :course/description {:db/doc "Optional Markdown description of the course's purpose and overall scope. Corresponds to the Course Description section in a course map; store the section body without its heading."}] [#edb/ref 1009 :course/overview {:db/doc "Optional Markdown overview of what students study and how the major areas connect, including teaching progression where established. Corresponds to the Course Overview section in a course map; store the section body without its heading."}] [#edb/ref 1010 :course-outcome/category {:db/doc "Optional category heading, for example Differentiation. Omit for an ungrouped outcome. This is a display grouping within the course, not a reference to a curriculum unit or module."}] [#edb/ref 1011 :course/school {:db/doc "Optional name of the school offering the course, for example Oregon State University."}] [#edb/ref 1012 :course/math-academy-id {:db/doc "Optional original Math Academy course identifier, taken from course-id in DATA/Courses.csv. Omit for independently created courses."}] [#edb/ref 1013 :course/code {:db/doc "Optional short course code, for example AG1 or MTH 255."}] [#edb/ref 1014 :course/id {:db/doc "Stable course identity assigned by our application, independent of Math Academy's identifier."}] [#edb/ref 1015 :course-outcome/id {:db/doc "Stable identity of a learning outcome owned by one course."}] [#edb/ref 1016 :course-outcome/text {:db/doc "The course-level capability stated by one outcome bullet, stored as Markdown supporting LaTeX. Excludes the bullet marker, category heading, and shared introductory sentence."}] [#edb/ref 1017 :unit/modules {:db/doc "Modules belonging to this unit. At least one is required when unit/validate is explicitly ensured. These ordinary refs define unordered membership; module/next supplies navigation between modules. Referenced modules must also ensure module/validate."}] [#edb/ref 1018 :unit/next {:db/doc "Optional direct downstream units for curriculum navigation. Ordinary refs preserve shared units; reverse lookup supplies preceding units. These links present progression between topic collections. Topic/next remains the authoritative prerequisite graph; unit links do not impose additional completion requirements."}] [#edb/ref 1019 :unit/math-academy-id {:db/doc "Optional original Math Academy unit identifier, taken from unit-id in DATA/Units.csv. Omit for independently created units."}] [#edb/ref 1020 :unit/id {:db/doc "Stable unit identity assigned by our application, independent of Math Academy's identifier and the unit's order within its course."}] [#edb/ref 1021 :unit/title {:db/doc "Unit title, taken from unit-name in DATA/Units.csv, for example Operations & Algebraic Thinking."}] [#edb/ref 1022 :module/next {:db/doc "Optional direct downstream modules for curriculum navigation. Ordinary refs preserve shared modules; reverse lookup supplies preceding modules. These links present progression between topic collections. Topic/next remains the authoritative prerequisite graph; module links do not impose additional completion requirements."}] [#edb/ref 1023 :module/topics {:db/doc "Topics belonging to this module. At least one is required when module/validate is explicitly ensured. These ordinary refs permit topic reuse across modules without cascading deletion. References define unordered membership; topic/next supplies direct downstream dependencies across the shared topic graph. Referenced topics must also ensure topic/validate."}] [#edb/ref 1024 :module/title {:db/doc "Module title, taken from module-name in DATA/Modules.csv, for example Operations on Numbers."}] [#edb/ref 1025 :module/math-academy-id {:db/doc "Optional original Math Academy module identifier, taken from module-id in DATA/Modules.csv. Omit for independently created modules."}] [#edb/ref 1026 :module/id {:db/doc "Stable module identity assigned by our application, independent of Math Academy's identifier and the module's order within its unit."}] [#edb/ref 1027 :topic/next {:db/doc "Direct downstream topics that require this topic. A next C means A is a direct prerequisite of C; reverse lookup of topics pointing to C supplies C's prerequisites. This is the authoritative topic dependency graph across all courses. Store direct edges; derive transitive dependencies by traversal. These ordinary refs do not establish ownership. Reference target types and prevention of self-dependencies and cycles require application validation. Distinct from encompassing weights and knowledge-point/key-prerequisites used for targeted remediation."}] [#edb/ref 1028 :topic/knowledge-points {:db/doc "Knowledge points taught within this topic; at least one is required when topic/validate is explicitly ensured. Their question pools are associated with the knowledge points. Instructional order will be defined separately; these references are unordered."}] [#edb/ref 1029 :topic/encompasses {:db/doc "Optional owned encompassing records, each identifying a component topic and its coverage weight. The containing topic supplies the source: practicing it exercises the referenced topics' skills. Defined in this file. Writers separately ensure encompassing/validate on each record. Relationships are distinct from prerequisites; duplicate targets, self-links, cycles, and ownership require additional validation."}] [#edb/ref 1030 :encompassing/weight {:db/doc "Coverage fraction from 0 to 1 describing how much practice the containing topic provides for the component topic. Distinct from learner accuracy and final repetition credit; the engine applies performance and timing rules separately."}] [#edb/ref 1031 :topic/title {:db/doc "Name of the topic, for example Integration by Substitution."}] [#edb/ref 1032 :encompassing/rationale {:db/doc "Optional explanation of which component skills the containing topic exercises and why this coverage weight was chosen."}] [#edb/ref 1033 :topic/math-academy-id {:db/doc "Optional original Math Academy topic identifier, taken from topic-id in DATA/Topics.csv or DATA/Lesson-Data tables. Omit for independently created topics."}] [#edb/ref 1034 :topic/difficulty {:db/doc "Optional positive finite lesson workload multiplier, default 1.0. Multiply the unrounded expected-distribution content score before rounding base XP. Calibrate from an authoritative Math Academy lesson base denominator and the first two questions per KP. Values above one are allowed. This is not accuracy and never enters retention or learning speed."}] [#edb/ref 1035 :topic/id {:db/doc "Stable topic identity, independent of its course memberships."}] [#edb/ref 1036 :encompassing/topic {:db/doc "The component topic whose skills are practiced implicitly. This ordinary ref preserves the topic when the encompassing record is deleted. Validate the referenced topic separately."}] [#edb/ref 1037 :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites {:db/doc "Optional references to prerequisite topics whose skills are most directly used in this KP, supporting targeted remedial reviews. Distinct from the containing topic's general prerequisites. These ordinary refs do not establish ownership; omit when no links are known."}] [#edb/ref 1038 :knowledge-point/questions {:db/doc "Required pool containing at least one ordinary gradable question associated with this KP. Any question referenced through knowledge-point/canonical-example is excluded, including examples of other KPs. Lesson practice, reviews, and assessments select appropriate items from the pool using learner history. This collection is unordered; question selection and avoidance of already-answered lesson items belong to the engine."}] [#edb/ref 1039 :knowledge-point/title {:db/doc "Name of the instructional skill or case demonstrated by the worked example, corresponding to captured example titles."}] [#edb/ref 1040 :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/doc "Optional reference to a question-generator entity holding a Python script that produces new questions for this KP. The application invokes the generator when more questions are needed, validates its output, and adds accepted questions to the KP's pool."}] [#edb/ref 1041 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/doc "Required reference to the canonical worked example question demonstrating this KP. The target must have question/id, a problem, and a nonempty worked solution. This reference establishes its worked-example role. This ordinary ref permits content reuse without cascading deletion. Canonical-example targets cannot belong to any KP practice question pool."}] [#edb/ref 1042 :knowledge-point/id {:db/doc "Stable identity of the knowledge point, independent of an individual learner's progress or question occurrences."}] [#edb/ref 1043 :activity/steps {:db/doc "Immediate steps owned by this activity. The collection is unordered; first-step and the steps' continuation links define the route. Steps inside referenced multistep content belong to that multistep instead. Validate steps and their referenced content separately."}] [#edb/ref 1044 :activity/type {:db/doc "Activity-type enum selecting the application's lesson, review, assessment, diagnostic, or assignment rules. An assignment may contain one multistep problem or several problems."}] [#edb/ref 1045 :activity/title {:db/doc "Display title of the activity."}] [#edb/ref 1046 :activity/first-step {:db/doc "Entry point into the activity; must be a member of activity/steps. This ordinary ref adds no second ownership relationship. Application stopping rules may finish an attempt before every step is presented."}] [#edb/ref 1047 :activity/due {:db/doc "Optional calendar deadline, such as an assignment due date. Distinct from a time limit measured after starting."}] [#edb/ref 1048 :activity/course {:db/doc "Optional course this activity belongs to, such as the school course assigning homework. References a course entity. Independent of the content targeted by activity/scope and assigned-problem/topic-coverage; does not restrict supporting topics to this course."}] [#edb/ref 1049 :activity/scope {:db/doc "Optional curriculum content targeted by this activity. Lessons and reviews target a topic; diagnostics may target a course, unit, module, or topic. Omit when scope is fully described by the selected content. Course affiliation belongs on activity/course; assignment problem coverage belongs on assigned-problem/topic-coverage. This ordinary ref preserves shared curriculum."}] [#edb/ref 1050 :activity/expected-seconds {:db/doc "Optional positive finite estimate of the activity's total working time, including adaptive practice. Omit when calculated directly from step estimates."}] [#edb/ref 1051 :activity/time-limit-seconds {:db/doc "Optional positive finite wall-clock limit for the whole activity, measured from the task's first start. Pausing does not extend this limit."}] [#edb/ref 1052 :activity/math-academy-id {:db/doc "Optional verified Math Academy activity-definition identifier. Captured taskId values belong on learner-task; do not substitute a topic or content ID."}] [#edb/ref 1053 :activity/id {:db/doc "Stable identity of the activity definition, independent of learner attempts."}] [#edb/ref 1054 :diagnostic-probe/on-correct {:db/doc "Next step in the same activity after a correct answer. Omit when this outcome ends the diagnostic."}] [#edb/ref 1055 :diagnostic-probe/on-incorrect {:db/doc "Next step in the same activity after an incorrect answer when no retry is taken. Omit when this outcome ends the diagnostic."}] [#edb/ref 1056 :diagnostic-probe/on-skipped {:db/doc "Next step in the same activity when the learner explicitly skips the presented question. Omit when this outcome ends the diagnostic. Unpresented questions do not take this branch."}] [#edb/ref 1057 :diagnostic-probe/on-silly-mistake {:db/doc "Optional alternate step in the same activity taken when the learner accepts a retry after a submitted incorrect answer. Use a different question on the same topic at the same difficulty, distinguishable from the ordinary incorrect continuation. The completed retry replaces the original result for frontier placement; both presentations remain in history. The application offers the available retry without a timing gate; skips receive no retry. Omit this branch on the alternate step to allow only one retry."}] [#edb/ref 1058 :step/next {:db/doc "Optional next sibling step under the same activity or multistep owner. The final inner step returns to the enclosing step's continuation. This is presentation order, not a prerequisite edge. Diagnostic steps use outcome branches instead of this linear continuation."}] [#edb/ref 1059 :step/expected-seconds {:db/doc "Optional positive finite expected workload for the whole stage, including any expanded practice. This estimate is not an enforced limit."}] [#edb/ref 1060 :step/time-limit-seconds {:db/doc "Optional positive finite maximum duration for the whole stage, including any expanded practice. Actual learner timing belongs to task records."}] [#edb/ref 1061 :step/math-academy-id {:db/doc "Optional verified Math Academy step or placement ID. Not a question or content ID."}] [#edb/ref 1062 :step/id {:db/doc "Stable identity of a stage in one activity or multistep problem."}] [#edb/ref 1063 :step/content {:db/doc "Tutorial, question (including a worked example), multistep, assigned problem, or knowledge point presented at this stage. An assigned problem references its question or multistep and carries its topic mapping. A multistep expands into its own steps; a knowledge point expands into its canonical example question and adaptive practice. Removing the step preserves its content."}] [#edb/ref 1064 :tutorial/content {:db/doc "Complete tutorial body as Markdown with LaTeX, tables, lists, and image links at their intended locations. Document order preserves the sequence of explanation, equations, and illustrations. Tutorials have no fixed problem/solution structure and do not require a gradable response."}] [#edb/ref 1065 :tutorial/math-academy-id {:db/doc "Optional MA tutorial content ID: contentid on a tutorial step in source HTML, or content_id in lesson JSON."}] [#edb/ref 1066 :tutorial/id {:db/doc "Stable identity of instructional content, independent of its placement in a lesson."}] [#edb/ref 1067 :tutorial/title {:db/doc "Title of the instructional section, such as Introduction or A Note on Differentiability."}] [#edb/ref 1068 :question/answer-fields {:db/doc "Owned answer fields. A question may mix radio, blank, select, checkbox, and free fields. Each blank/select has its own key and bank. Each authored checkbox option has its own field, key, two text answers true/false, and one canonical answer. All required fields together form one question; grading produces one question correctness observation. Free fields collect responses and may reveal an optional reference without automatic correctness evidence. Fieldless school prompts remain displayable without grading or mastery credit."}] [#edb/ref 1069 :question/math-academy-id {:db/doc "Optional prefixed Math Academy content identifier: q-N for a source question ID or e-N for a source example content ID. The prefixes prevent overlap in this unique attribute. Identifies content, not a presentation or learner attempt. Omit for independently created content."}] [#edb/ref 1070 :question/difficulty {:db/doc "Optional reference to an E/M/H difficulty enum entity observed in completed MA activity: :question.difficulty/easy, /moderate, or /hard. This is distinct from aggregate topic difficulty and learner ability. Omit when unknown; allowed values require validation."}] [#edb/ref 1071 :question/problem {:db/doc "Problem statement, stored as Markdown supporting LaTeX and image links. For gradable questions, named field locations correspond to answer-field/key on this question's fields. For examples, this is the demonstrated problem."}] [#edb/ref 1072 :question/id {:db/doc "Stable identity of a question or worked example. Individual presentations and submissions have separate identities; changing option order does not create a new question."}] [#edb/ref 1073 :question/requires-calculator {:db/doc "Whether a calculator is required to answer the question. Captured MA instructions all express a requirement, sometimes specifying a scientific or graphing calculator. This boolean records the requirement only