earner-entered strings are retained verbatim, including empty or malformed math input. Authored math values may use LaTeX without Markdown delimiters; text and image values hold their respective content. Evaluation and normalization are separate from storage."}] [#edb/ref 1081 :answer/feedback {:db/doc "Optional feedback associated with this answer value, such as an explanation for a radio or select option."}] [#edb/ref 1082 :answer/type {:db/doc "Representation: answer.type/math, answer.type/text, or answer.type/image."}] [#edb/ref 1083 :answer/id {:db/doc "Stable identity of a field-scoped answer value. Reuse this entity for repeated identical values within its field; do not share it across fields."}] [#edb/ref 1084 :multistep/steps {:db/doc "Immediate generic steps owned by this problem. The collection is unordered; first-step and step/next define presentation order. Do not also add these steps to the enclosing activity's steps."}] [#edb/ref 1085 :multistep/context {:db/doc "Optional shared setup, data, diagrams, or instructions in Markdown with LaTeX and image links. Kept available throughout this problem's parts; omit when parts share no setup."}] [#edb/ref 1086 :multistep/id {:db/doc "Stable identity of a reusable multipart problem."}] [#edb/ref 1087 :multistep/first-step {:db/doc "Starting step; must be a member of multistep/steps. This ordinary ref adds no second ownership relationship."}] [#edb/ref 1088 :assigned-problem/topic-coverage {:db/doc "Optional mapped topics needed for this problem. The scheduler combines these targets with the enclosing assignment's deadline and learner progress to prioritize preparation. Derive prerequisites from topic/next. Absent coverage means the problem is not yet mapped; coverage does not establish question-bank membership or award mastery."}] [#edb/ref 1089 :assigned-problem/content {:db/doc "Question or multistep containing the problem itself. This ordinary ref preserves reusable content when the assigned-problem entity is removed."}] [#edb/ref 1090 :assigned-problem/id {:db/doc "Stable identity of an externally supplied problem, independent of its placement in an assignment."}] [#edb/ref 1091 :policy/question-selection-weights {:db/doc "Optional owned question-weight records, defined in 2-question-weights.edn. Each record supplies initial and remedial difficulty distributions for one activity type. Keep at most one record per activity type in this policy; find the policy through the reverse ref. Ensure question-weights/validate on each child. Selection and missing-configuration handling belong to application code."}] [#edb/ref 1092 :policy/maximum-half-life-days {:db/doc "Finite upper bound on retention half-life, at least base-half-life-days."}] [#edb/ref 1093 :policy/maximum-failure-multiplier {:db/doc "Finite upper bound on the failure penalty multiplier; at least one."}] [#edb/ref 1094 :policy/maximum-speed {:db/doc "Finite upper bound on the repetition-credit multiplier; at least one."}] [#edb/ref 1095 :policy/interval-growth {:db/doc "Half-life multiplier per unit of repetition credit. Must be finite and greater than one."}] [#edb/ref 1096 :policy/speed-exponent {:db/doc "Nonnegative finite exponent controlling the effect of learner accuracy and topic difficulty on repetition credit."}] [#edb/ref 1097 :policy/future-horizon-days {:db/doc "Nonnegative finite horizon used to compare how much candidate activities postpone upcoming reviews."}] [#edb/ref 1098 :policy/overdue-failure-slope {:db/doc "Nonnegative finite rate at which the failure penalty increases with overdue half-lives."}] [#edb/ref 1099 :policy/description {:db/doc "Optional explanation of the settings and their intended use."}] [#edb/ref 1100 :policy/early-practice-discount-power {:db/doc "Positive exponent controlling how repetition credit increases as retention falls toward the review threshold."}] [#edb/ref 1101 :policy/minimum-speed {:db/doc "Positive lower bound on the repetition-credit multiplier; at most one."}] [#edb/ref 1102 :policy/initial-retention {:db/doc "Retention score assigned on initial learning and reference level used to discount early practice. Positive and finite; later practice can produce a larger score."}] [#edb/ref 1103 :policy/review-threshold {:db/doc "Retention score at or below which an established topic is due for review. Positive and below initial-retention; not a recall probability."}] [#edb/ref 1104 :policy/id {:db/doc "Stable identity of this parameter set. Edit its settings under this identity; retained EDB history records previous values. Independent of the engine runtime fingerprint."}] [#edb/ref 1105 :policy/initial-accuracy {:db/doc "Starting accuracy when learner evidence is unavailable; also the default topic difficulty and normalization baseline in the current FIRe model. Strictly between zero and one."}] [#edb/ref 1106 :policy/base-half-life-days {:db/doc "Starting retention half-life in days before repetition credit increases it. Must be finite and positive."}] [#edb/ref 1107 :policy/retention-update-order {:db/doc "Supported update order: policy.retention-update/decay-before-add or /add-before-decay. The engine applies the selected ordering explicitly."}] [#edb/ref 1108 :policy/accuracy-update-rate {:db/doc "Weight assigned to a new direct answer in the accuracy estimate. Greater than zero and at most one; fractional evidence adjusts this rate in application code."}] [#edb/ref 1109 :policy/gate-slow-implicit {:db/doc "Whether positive implicit retention credit is withheld when the topic repetition-credit multiplier is below one."}] [#edb/ref 1110 :question-weights/activity-type {:db/doc "Activity-type enum selecting the distribution's use, initially activity.type/lesson or activity.type/review. Reuses the enums defined in content/0-activity.edn."}] [#edb/ref 1111 :question-weights/initial-easy {:db/doc "Relative weight for choosing Easy questions in the initial set. Must be finite and nonnegative; zero excludes this band."}] [#edb/ref 1112 :question-weights/remedial-easy {:db/doc "Relative weight for choosing Easy questions in the remedial set. Must be finite and nonnegative; zero excludes this band."}] [#edb/ref 1113 :question-weights/initial-hard {:db/doc "Relative weight for choosing Hard questions in the initial set. Must be finite and nonnegative; zero excludes this band."}] [#edb/ref 1114 :question-weights/remedial-hard {:db/doc "Relative weight for choosing Hard questions in the remedial set. Must be finite and nonnegative; zero excludes this band."}] [#edb/ref 1115 :question-weights/initial-moderate {:db/doc "Relative weight for choosing Moderate questions in the initial set. Must be finite and nonnegative; zero excludes this band."}] [#edb/ref 1116 :question-weights/remedial-moderate {:db/doc "Relative weight for choosing Moderate questions in the remedial set. Must be finite and nonnegative; zero excludes this band."}] [#edb/ref 1117 :learner/assignments {:db/doc "Assignments associated with this learner. References activities whose activity/type is activity.type/assignment."}] [#edb/ref 1118 :learner/targets {:db/doc "Longer-term study destinations selected by the learner, displayed with their prerequisite graph. These ordinary refs point to shared topics across courses. Immediate self-directed activities come from learner/queue. Removing a target preserves its topic and all learner history."}] [#edb/ref 1119 :learner/activity {:db/doc "Optional collection of learner-specific tasks, including attempts and their history. Each task references a shared activity definition and records its status, elapsed working time, and XP. Status includes completed and failed; there is no separate task outcome. Tasks are defined in 3-learner-task.edn and own the items defined in 3-learner-task.edn. Calendar timestamps and history order come from status transactions. Validate each task and its learner association separately. These ordinary refs do not establish component ownership."}] [#edb/ref 1120 :learner/knowledge-profile {:db/doc "Owned, unordered collection of current progress records, one per topic. Find the learner through the reverse reference learner/_knowledge-profile. Ensure learner/validate when changing membership. Partial imports may contain only known progress facts; ensure progress/validate when writing complete operational state for the engine. Retracting the learner also retracts these records, but not their shared topics."}] [#edb/ref 1121 :learner/queue {:db/doc "Unordered topics explicitly selected by the learner for self-directed study. References shared topics across courses. Adding a topic requests preparation from its existing database lesson content regardless of the selected Study mode. When learner/self-directed is true, Study serves these prepared activities even without engine prerequisite eligibility, without marking them unlocked. Ongoing attempts come first, followed by lower global topic/next layers and then higher scheduling priority within a layer. An empty queue does not fall back to engine recommendations. These ordinary refs do not establish ownership. Removing a queued topic preserves the topic and all learner history. Distinct from learner/targets, which records longer-term study destinations."}] [#edb/ref 1122 :performance/assessment-accuracy {:db/doc "Learner-global assessment-only exponentially weighted accuracy in [0,1]. Equal averaging with practice accuracy is described publicly; the precise update rate and prior are local parameters. Update from direct observed answers once, not from every propagated topic update."}] [#edb/ref 1123 :performance/practice-accuracy {:db/doc "Learner-global non-assessment exponentially weighted accuracy in [0,1], kept separate so repeated lesson/review work does not swamp assessment evidence. Update from direct observed answers once, not from every propagated topic update."}] [#edb/ref 1124 :performance/assessment-mass {:db/doc "Learner-global nonnegative effective assessment evidence mass under the local update, distinct from assessment accuracy. Update from direct observed answers once, not from every propagated topic update."}] [#edb/ref 1125 :performance/practice-mass {:db/doc "Learner-global nonnegative effective non-assessment evidence mass under the local update, distinct from practice accuracy. Update from direct observed answers once, not from every propagated topic update."}] [#edb/ref 1126 :learner/course {:db/doc "Optional course currently selected in the UI. References a shared course entity."}] [#edb/ref 1127 :learner/performance {:db/doc "Optional owned overall performance record, defined in 1-learner.edn. Holds accuracy and evidence mass across topics. Find its learner through learner/_performance; no duplicate learner ref is needed. Ensure performance/validate separately on each performance write. Retracting the learner also retracts this record."}] [#edb/ref 1128 :learner/id {:db/doc "Stable learner identity used by the FIRe engine; not a login credential."}] [#edb/ref 1129 :learner/name {:db/doc "The learner's display name."}] [#edb/ref 1130 :learner/self-directed {:db/doc "Whether Study uses the learner's explicitly selected topic queue instead of engine recommendations. Applications should treat an absent value as false."}] [#edb/ref 1131 :progress/assessment-accuracy {:db/doc "Assessment-only exponentially weighted accuracy in [0,1]. Equal averaging with practice accuracy is described publicly; the precise update rate and prior are local parameters."}] [#edb/ref 1132 :progress/topic {:db/doc "Existing topic entity, shared across course contexts."}] [#edb/ref 1133 :progress/last-direct-at {:db/doc "Last direct qualifying practice time, when known; implicit credit does not replace it."}] [#edb/ref 1134 :progress/practice-accuracy {:db/doc "Non-assessment exponentially weighted accuracy in [0,1], kept separate so repeated lesson/review work does not swamp assessment evidence."}] [#edb/ref 1135 :progress/assessment-mass {:db/doc "Nonnegative effective assessment evidence mass under the local update, distinct from assessment accuracy."}] [#edb/ref 1136 :progress/practice-mass {:db/doc "Nonnegative effective non-assessment evidence mass under the local update."}] [#edb/ref 1137 :progress/repetitions {:db/doc "Nonnegative fractional repetition position. Operational state is clamped at zero; it is not an integer count of reviews."}] [#edb/ref 1138 :progress/memory {:db/doc "Nonnegative model memory value anchored at memory-at. It is not a probability and need not be at most one."}] [#edb/ref 1139 :progress/expected-assessment-accuracy {:db/doc "Optional initial assessment accuracy forecast in [0,1], frozen before the first local outcome. Direct prerequisite assessment accuracies are weighted by their positive assessment masses; fallback is the learner's mass-weighted topic assessment accuracy, then policy/initial-accuracy. This forecast creates no evidence and does not overwrite observed accuracy. Backfilled values are migration-time estimates."}] [#edb/ref 1140 :progress/expected-practice-accuracy {:db/doc "Optional initial practice accuracy forecast in [0,1], frozen before the first local outcome. Direct prerequisite practice accuracies are weighted by their positive practice masses; fallback is the learner's mass-weighted topic practice accuracy, then policy/initial-accuracy. Separate from assessment and from the shared topic workload multiplier. Backfilled values are migration-time estimates."}] [#edb/ref 1141 :progress/policy {:db/doc "Policy used to compute this state, identified by policy/id. Historical reads at the state-change transaction recover the settings used then; current policy values may have been adjusted since."}] [#edb/ref 1142 :progress/interval-days {:db/doc "Positive finite interval used to decay this anchored memory until the next update. The local interval function determines its value."}] [#edb/ref 1143 :progress/id {:db/doc "Stable state identity; update it rather than creating another profile for the same learner-topic pair."}] [#edb/ref 1144 :progress/memory-at {:db/doc "Time at which the stored memory value applies. Compute elapsed days from this anchor once."}] [#edb/ref 1145 :progress/learned {:db/doc "Whether this topic is admitted to retention tracking after a mastery-learning or explicit initialization decision. True alone does not establish current recall."}] [#edb/ref 1146 :task-item/responses {:db/doc "Answer entities submitted for this question: entered blank/free values, selected radio/select options, and explicit true or false answers for every checkbox field. Unchecked checkbox options submit false and are not unanswered. Recover each answer's field through reverse answer-field/choices ownership. At most one response per field; identical typed entered values are reused within that field and original strings are preserved. These ordinary refs do not own answers. A free response does not itself assert correct or incorrect."}] [#edb/ref 1147 :learner-task/items {:db/doc "Owned question, tutorial, and example presentations, linked in order through task-item/next. The reference collection itself is unordered. Repeated presentations have separate item identities."}] [#edb/ref 1148 :task-item/elapsed-seconds {:db/doc "Accumulated seconds spent in started, calculated from this item's status transaction history. Paused intervals are excluded. The application updates this value and the parent task's elapsed total together, with at most one actively timed item per learner. Imported observed durations may be retained when their status history is unavailable."}] [#edb/ref 1149 :learner-task/elapsed-seconds {:db/doc "Accumulated working seconds, calculated by summing task-item/elapsed-seconds across this task's items. The application updates this total with the item durations; it is not an independently edited value or the timed-exam deadline. Omit when durations are unknown."}] [#edb/ref 1150 :task-item/deferred-step {:db/doc "Authored knowledge-point stage deferred after this completed example or answered question because no fresh gradable questions were available. Keeps the practice unfinished while later lesson stages proceed; never a skip, failure, or mastery assertion. Application validates same-activity membership and exhaustion."}] [#edb/ref 1151 :task-item/resumed-step {:db/doc "Authored knowledge-point stage revisited by this canonical-example presentation after finishing a lesson route with deferred practice. Replay resumes only outstanding stages and retains prior question outcomes and exposure history. Application validates that the stage was deferred in this task."}] [#edb/ref 1152 :task-item/performance {:db/doc "Calculated performance magnitude used by the engine. Positive and finite; may exceed one. Distinct from correctness and XP. Omit until evaluated; the application checks the range."}] [#edb/ref 1153 :learner-task/status {:db/doc "Locked means not yet eligible for an engine-selected start; unlocked means engine-eligible but not started. Explicit self-directed queue selections may start a prepared locked task directly without an intermediate unlock. Preparation does not start a clock or establish mastery. Started means in progress; paused means suspended and unfinished, including a lesson route whose completed presentations retain deferred practice markers while waiting for fresh questions. Completed means finished under the activity's completion rules; failed means an explicit task-level failure condition ended the attempt. Status transaction history supplies calendar timestamps, including the first start and terminal transition. Pausing does not extend a timed exam's deadline. Question correctness is recorded by task-item/status; no separate task outcome is stored."}] [#edb/ref 1154 :learner-task/priority {:db/doc "Numerical scheduling priority; higher values are served first. Eligible unfinished tasks at or above the application's threshold are required. The application calculates finite values and defines the scale and threshold."}] [#edb/ref 1155 :learner-task/math-academy-id {:db/doc "Optional Math Academy taskId. Reconcile within the learner's history; global uniqueness across learners is not established."}] [#edb/ref 1156 :task-item/next {:db/doc "Optional next presentation in the same learner task. Omit on the last item. This ordinary ref orders the task's existing members; learner-task/items remains their component owner. Derive the first item from the member with no incoming next link. The application checks that all members form one chain without cycles, merges, or links outside the task."}] [#edb/ref 1157 :learner-task/xp-base {:db/doc "Optional nonnegative baseline XP for this attempt, before bonuses or penalties. The displayed denominator is not a maximum."}] [#edb/ref 1158 :task-item/content {:db/doc "Question, worked example question, or tutorial presented. May be absent when historical content identity is unknown."}] [#edb/ref 1159 :learner-task/activity {:db/doc "Shared activity definition for this learner task. Resolve its title, type, and intended scope through this reference."}] [#edb/ref 1160 :learner-task/id {:db/doc "Stable identity of this attempt, independent of external identifiers."}] [#edb/ref 1161 :task-item/id {:db/doc "Stable identity of this presentation, separate from the content ID."}] [#edb/ref 1162 :task-item/status {:db/doc "Started means actively working; paused suspends the working timer. Completed ends a tutorial, worked example, or submitted question containing free fields whose responses are saved without automatic grading. Correct, incorrect, and skipped end automatically evaluated ordinary question attempts. Retained status history supplies timing. Free response completion does not assert correctness, performance, or mastery credit. Questions never presented do not create task items. Valid transitions and type-specific completion require application validation."}] [#edb/ref 1163 :learner-task/xp-earned {:db/doc "XP awarded for this attempt, including penalties and bonuses. May be negative or exceed xp-base. Omit when unknown."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045416 :person/jake {:db/doc "Jake"}] [#edb/ref 17592186045417 :org/Math-Academy {:db/doc "Math Academy"}] [#edb/ref 17592186045418 :org/Oregon-State {:db/doc "Oregon State University"}] [#edb/ref 17592186045419 :agent/gpt-6-astra-high {:db/doc "GPT-6 Astra — high reasoning effort (Codex configuration)."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045420 :agent/gpt-6-astra-low {:db/doc "GPT-6 Astra — low reasoning effort (Codex configuration)."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045421 :agent/gpt-6-astra-max {:db/doc "GPT-6 Astra — max reasoning effort (Codex configuration)."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045422 :agent/gpt-6-astra-medium {:db/doc "GPT-6 Astra — medium reasoning effort (Codex configuration)."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045423 :agent/gpt-6-astra-ultra {:db/doc "GPT-6 Astra — ultra reasoning effort (Codex configuration)."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045424 :agent/gpt-6-astra-xhigh {:db/doc "GPT-6 Astra — xhigh reasoning effort (Codex configuration)."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045425 :agent/gpt-6-luna-high {:db/doc "GPT-6 Luna — high reasoning effort (Codex configuration)."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045426 :agent/gpt-6-luna-low {:db/doc "GPT-6 Luna — low reasoning effort (Codex configuration)."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045427 :agent/gpt-6-luna-max {:db/doc "GPT-6 Luna — max reasoning effort (Codex configuration)."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045428 :agent/gpt-6-luna-medium {:db/doc "GPT-6 Luna — medium reasoning effort (Codex configuration)."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045429 :agent/gpt-6-luna-xhigh {:db/doc "GPT-6 Luna — xhigh reasoning effort (Codex configuration)."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045430 :agent/gpt-6-sol-high {:db/doc "GPT-6 Sol — high reasoning effort (Codex configuration)."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045431 :agent/gpt-6-sol-low {:db/doc "GPT-6 Sol — low reasoning effort (Codex configuration)."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045432 :agent/gpt-6-sol-max {:db/doc "GPT-6 Sol — max reasoning effort (Codex configuration)."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045433 :agent/gpt-6-sol-medium {:db/doc "GPT-6 Sol — medium reasoning effort (Codex configuration)."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045434 :agent/gpt-6-sol-ultra {:db/doc "GPT-6 Sol — ultra reasoning effort (Codex configuration)."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045435 :agent/gpt-6-sol-xhigh {:db/doc "GPT-6 Sol — xhigh reasoning effort (Codex configuration)."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045436 :agent/gpt-6.1-sol-high {:db/doc "GPT-6.1 Sol — high reasoning effort (Codex configuration)."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045437 :agent/gpt-6.1-sol-low {:db/doc "GPT-6.1 Sol — low reasoning effort (Codex configuration)."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045438 :agent/gpt-6.1-sol-max {:db/doc "GPT-6.1 Sol — max reasoning effort (Codex configuration)."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045439 :agent/gpt-6.1-sol-medium {:db/doc "GPT-6.1 Sol — medium reasoning effort (Codex configuration)."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045440 :agent/gpt-6.1-sol-ultra {:db/doc "GPT-6.1 Sol — ultra reasoning effort (Codex configuration)."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045441 :agent/gpt-6.1-sol-xhigh {:db/doc "GPT-6.1 Sol — xhigh reasoning effort (Codex configuration)."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045442 :agent/chatgpt-6-pro {:db/doc "ChatGPT 6 Pro — course-map author identified from Jake's recollection; exact model not recorded in the saved export."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045443 :application/ca-engine {:db/doc "Course Academy engine."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045444 :course-group/validate {:db/doc "Requires identity, title, and at least one course ref when explicitly ensured. Nonempty titles and reference target types require application validation."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045445 :course-outcome/validate {:db/doc "Requires identity, index, and outcome text when explicitly ensured. Category is optional. Nonempty text and category labels, positive indexes, index uniqueness within the course, and ownership by exactly one course require additional validation."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045446 :course/identity-validate {:db/doc "Requires only identity for a placeholder course when explicitly ensured. Use course/validate after filling in its required data."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045447 :course/validate {:db/doc "Requires our identity, a title, and at least one unit ref when explicitly ensured. The Math Academy identifier, course code, school, description, overview, outcomes, and next courses are optional. Nonempty titles, reference target types, outcome indexes unique within this course, and prevention of self-links and cycles require application validation."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045448 :unit/identity-validate {:db/doc "Requires only identity for a placeholder unit when explicitly ensured. Use unit/validate after filling in its required data."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045449 :unit/validate {:db/doc "Requires our identity, a title, and at least one module ref when explicitly ensured. The Math Academy identifier and next units are optional. Nonempty titles, reference target types, and prevention of self-links and cycles require application validation. Referenced modules must be validated separately."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045450 :module/identity-validate {:db/doc "Requires only identity for a placeholder module when explicitly ensured. Use module/validate after filling in its required data."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045451 :module/validate {:db/doc "Requires our identity, a title, and at least one topic ref when explicitly ensured. The Math Academy identifier and next modules are optional. Nonempty titles, reference target types, and prevention of self-links and cycles require application validation. Referenced topics must be validated separately."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045452 :topic/validate {:db/doc "A curricular topic, shared across courses and containing knowledge points. Explicit db/ensure requires identity, title, and at least one knowledge-point reference. The predicate checks difficulty when present. Referenced knowledge points and encompassing records must be validated separately."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045453 :encompassing/validate {:db/doc "Requires a component topic and weight when explicitly ensured. A valid topic target, finite weight in [0,1], and relationship consistency require additional validation."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045454 :topic/difficulty-validate {:db/doc "Requires a topic identity and a strictly positive finite workload multiplier. Does not require a fully populated curriculum topic."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045455 :topic/identity-validate {:db/doc "Requires only identity for a placeholder topic when explicitly ensured. Use topic/validate after filling in its required data."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045456 :knowledge-point/validate {:db/doc "Native EDB specification requiring KP identity, title, a canonical example question ref, and at least one practice question ref when explicitly ensured. Writers ensure question/validate for both examples and practice questions, along with child specifications. The application checks target types, nonempty canonical worked solutions, disjointness of all canonical targets from every practice pool, mathematical correctness, and selection rules."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045457 :knowledge-point/identity-validate {:db/doc "Requires only identity for a placeholder knowledge point when explicitly ensured. Use knowledge-point/validate after filling in its required data."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045459 :activity/validate {:db/doc "Requires identity, title, type, steps, and an entry point. The application checks enum values, step ownership and routing, positive finite timings, and type-specific requirements: topic scope for lessons/reviews and curriculum scope for diagnostics. Assignment deadlines are optional."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045460 :activity.type/assessment {}] [#edb/ref 17592186045461 :activity.type/assignment {}] [#edb/ref 17592186045462 :activity.type/diagnostic {}] [#edb/ref 17592186045463 :activity.type/lesson {}] [#edb/ref 17592186045464 :activity.type/review {}] [#edb/ref 17592186045470 :step/validate {:db/doc "Requires identity and content when explicitly ensured. The application checks exactly one owner through activity/steps or multistep/steps, reference targets, positive finite timings, and valid continuation links. Containment must be acyclic. Validate content separately."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045480 :tutorial/validate {:db/doc "Native EDB specification requiring identity, title, and instructional content when explicitly ensured. Nonempty content, valid assets, and mathematical correctness require additional validation."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045484 :question/validate {:db/doc "Requires identity and problem when explicitly ensured. The application requires complete answer fields before automatic grading, and a worked solution for canonical examples, validates any present fields and answer values, and derives example roles from knowledge-point/canonical-example and excludes those targets from every practice pool. A fieldless school problem may be displayed through assigned-problem without grading or awarding mastery."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045485 :question.difficulty/easy {}] [#edb/ref 17592186045486 :question.difficulty/hard {}] [#edb/ref 17592186045487 :question.difficulty/moderate {}] [#edb/ref 17592186045491 :answer-field/validate {:db/doc "Requires identity, key, and type when explicitly ensured. The type-specific predicate validates owned answer values and canonical membership. Radio, select, blank, and checkbox require a nonempty bank and one canonical answer. Free permits an empty bank and no reference answer. Checkbox banks contain exactly two text answers, true and false. Writers also ensure answer/validate. Question field-key uniqueness, immutable referenced values, entered-answer reuse, and response completeness require application handling."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045492 :answer-field.type/blank {}] [#edb/ref 17592186045493 :answer-field.type/radio {}] [#edb/ref 17592186045494 :answer-field.type/select {}] [#edb/ref 17592186045496 :answer/validate {:db/doc "Requires identity, type, and a string value when explicitly ensured. The application checks supported answer types and field-scoped deduplication, keeps referenced values immutable, and may validate authored image availability. Do not reject an entered value solely because its math syntax is malformed."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045497 :answer.type/image {}] [#edb/ref 17592186045498 :answer.type/math {}] [#edb/ref 17592186045499 :answer.type/text {}] [#edb/ref 17592186045500 :multistep/validate {:db/doc "Requires identity, steps, and an entry point. The application checks single step ownership, a connected acyclic sibling sequence, and acyclic content nesting. Validate steps and their content separately."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045504 :assigned-problem/validate {:db/doc "Requires identity and content when explicitly ensured. Coverage may be added later. The application checks that content references a question or multistep and coverage references topics; validate the referenced content separately."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045507 :policy/validate {:db/doc "Requires identity and all FIRe retention settings. The registered predicate checks the update-order enum, finite numeric ranges, and relationships between those settings. Optional question-selection records require their own validation; the application checks their ownership and unique activity types. Formulas and applying changed settings to existing progress belong to application code."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045508 :policy.retention-update/add-before-decay {}] [#edb/ref 17592186045509 :policy.retention-update/decay-before-add {}] [#edb/ref 17592186045526 :question-weights/validate {:db/doc "Requires an activity type and all six weights when explicitly ensured. The application checks allowed activity types, finite nonnegative weights, a positive finite total for each distribution, exactly one policy owner, and one record per activity type in that policy. Weights are normalized across eligible bands before selecting a fresh question within the chosen band; an unavailable question supply is not learner failure. Stopping rules remain application code."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045533 :xp-weights/lesson-v1 {:db/doc "Completed lesson: if p < 0.50, XP = -1; else if p = 1, XP = R(1.25 B); else XP = R(B min(1, 1.5 p - 0.30)). Use all ordinary question occurrences across the task, not average per-KP accuracy. A failed completed task still receives this formula's award; unfinished tasks receive no final award."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045534 :xp-weights/multistep-v1 {:db/doc "Completed multistep activity: XP = max(-1, R(B (2.25 p - 1))). Count ordinary question occurrences once regardless of answer-field count. Perfect work earns R(1.25 B). The negative floor applies after rounding."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045535 :xp-weights/assessment-v1 {:db/doc "Completed or expired quiz/assessment: p < 0.20 -> -1; otherwise max(0, R(1.20 B (p - 0.35) / 0.65)). N is the full assigned question count; C counts correct submissions. Unanswered questions receive no correct credit. Perfect work earns R(1.20 B). Diagnostic placement is a separate policy and does not use this rule."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045536 :xp-weights/review-v1 {:db/doc "Completed review, in order: p < 0.50 -> -1; p = 1 -> B + 2; p >= 2/3 -> B; otherwise final ordinary question incorrect/skipped -> 0; otherwise R(B p). The final outcome must be known in the partial-credit band. The perfect bonus is additive two XP, not a percentage."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045537 :learner/validate {:db/doc "Learner identity and knowledge-profile ownership/uniqueness. Overall performance is optional and its child record must be separately ensured with performance/validate. This spec does not validate performance ownership or values."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045538 :performance/validate {:db/doc "Requires all four values for the complete overall performance estimate. Effective accuracy is the mean of the two accuracy fields; do not persist another independently mutable copy. The writer checks exactly one learner owner, finite accuracy in [0,1], and finite nonnegative evidence mass. Update the existing child through learner/performance rather than replacing it for each observation."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045547 :progress/validate {:db/doc "Requires one learner owner, one record per topic in that profile, and complete operational state. Ability can exist while learned=false, including after failed initial lessons. Effective accuracy is the mean of the two accuracy strata. Initialization values are explicit local choices, not inferred from XP."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045562 :learner-task/validate {:db/doc "Requires identity, activity, and lifecycle state. The application checks one learner association, valid content, enums, and timing; validate child records separately."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045563 :task-item/validate {:db/doc "Requires presentation identity and status. The next link is optional; historical content may be unknown. Task membership, chain consistency, status transitions, and derived elapsed totals require application validation."}] [#edb/ref 17592186045564 :learner-task.status/completed {}] [#edb/ref 17592186045565 :learner-task.status/failed {}] [#edb/ref 17592186045566 :learner-task.status/locked {}] [#edb/ref 17592186045567 :learner-task.status/paused {}] [#edb/ref 17592186045568 :learner-task.status/started {}] [#edb/ref 17592186045569 :learner-task.status/unlocked {}] [#edb/ref 17592186045570 :task-item.status/completed {}] [#edb/ref 17592186045571 :task-item.status/correct {}] [#edb/ref 17592186045572 :task-item.status/incorrect {}] [#edb/ref 17592186045573 :task-item.status/paused {}] [#edb/ref 17592186045574 :task-item.status/skipped {}] [#edb/ref 17592186045575 :task-item.status/started {}] [#edb/ref 17592186408166 :answer-field.type/checkbox {}] [#edb/ref 17592186408167 :answer-field.type/free {}]}
